  "spec_section": "markdown-dialect.md §3.1 / §3.2 / §3.7.5 / §6",
  "description": "Pins the Myne dialect `%%…%%` editor-only comment (markdown-dialect.md §3.2 inline / §3.1 block, MYND-315): recognition (inline + multi-line block, terminated-only), the structural exclusion zones (§3.7.5: code fence / inline code / wikilink / math leaf — no comment recognized there), the terminated-vs-unterminated tie-break (an unterminated `%%` is INERT — no node, stays literal text, a deliberate divergence from Obsidian's unterminated-`%%`-swallows-to-EOF behavior), and the canonical comment-STRIP output every lossy projection (HTML / PDF / stripped-TXT / document statistics) shares (the pure recognize-strip pass that removes each recognized comment node's byte range, all other bytes verbatim). The `.md` export is byte-verbatim and does NOT strip (SYNC-2) — only lossy projections strip. Deterministic cross-client behavior in the property-coercion / note-template class (not a codec, not cryptographic). property-index is single-authority for typing; this category is single-authority for `%%` recognition + strip. Hand-curated against §3.1/§3.2/§3.7.5/§6; the desktop Vitest runner asserts the live TS recognizer + strip against these vectors. A failing vector in any port is a stop-the-world bug.",
